Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: power down the SDIO combo in suspend on RG353PS

The shared RGxx3 device tree keeps the RTL8821CS rail always-on and asks the
MMC core to keep the SDIO card powered across system suspend. That leaves the
radio energised for the whole sleep window, which is the largest single
contributor to the board's suspend current and provides no benefit: there is
no wake-on-wireless on this handheld.

regulator-state-mem cannot be used for this rail because regulator-fixed does
not implement set_suspend_disable(), so __suspend_set_state() silently does
nothing. Removing "regulator-always-on" turns the rail into a normal
switchable regulator, and removing "keep-power-in-suspend" makes
mmc_sdio_suspend() call mmc_power_off(), which disables vmmc and drives the
enable GPIO low.

The SDIO card is therefore re-enumerated on resume and rtw88 has to reload its
firmware; this needs hardware verification.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-anbernic-rg353ps.dts
--- 
@@ -114,3 +114,28 @@
 		rockchip,sleep-filter-current-microamp = <100000>;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Deep suspend: power the RTL8821CS combo off.
+ *
+ * rk3566-anbernic-rgxx3.dtsi keeps vcc_wifi always-on and asks the MMC core
+ * to keep the SDIO card powered across suspend. Both together leave the radio
+ * energised for the whole suspend window, which dominates the board's sleep
+ * current and buys nothing: this handheld has no wake-on-wireless.
+ *
+ * reg- lator-state-mem cannot help here - regulator-fixed has no
+ * set_suspend_disable op, so __suspend_set_state() silently does nothing.
+ * Dropping "always-on" instead makes the rail a normal switchable regulator,
+ * and dropping "keep-power-in-suspend" makes mmc_sdio_suspend() call
+ * mmc_power_off(), which disables vmmc and drives the enable GPIO low.
+ *
+ * Consequence to verify on hardware: the card is re-enumerated on resume and
+ * rtw88 reloads its firmware. Keep the output quiet only if that works.
+ */
+&vcc_wifi {
+	/delete-property/ regulator-always-on;
+};
+
+&sdmmc2 {
+	/delete-property/ keep-power-in-suspend;
+};
